WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.589 --> 00:00:05.939
I think of human flourishing as living well.

00:00:05.939 --> 00:00:09.680
Maybe a question we've all asked is: What
is the good life?

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:11.300
What does it mean to live well?

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:15.220
And that's a question that philosophers as
well as people like you and me have asked

00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:20.039
over the centuries, right?

00:00:20.039 --> 00:00:22.490
Aristotle had an interesting answer to that
question.

00:00:22.490 --> 00:00:29.020
Aristotle would say that people flourish when
they exercise virtue.

00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:32.879
And virtues are things like wisdom and courage.

00:00:32.879 --> 00:00:38.690
So if you think of a virtue like courage,
then flourishing — it happens when you exercise

00:00:38.690 --> 00:00:43.340
courage even in the most difficult circumstances.

00:00:43.340 --> 00:00:49.720
So it's possible to flourish even if you are
going through something really hard.

00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:56.580
I would say mathematics is actually a vehicle
for helping people flourish.

00:00:56.580 --> 00:01:02.180
If you think about what it means to do mathematics,
part of what you're trying to do in mathematics

00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:04.089
is seek truth.

00:01:04.089 --> 00:01:09.799
In seeking truth you build in abilities — virtues
— of rigorous thinking, handling ideas well,

00:01:09.799 --> 00:01:12.249
being intellectually honest.

00:01:12.249 --> 00:01:17.679
If you think about what it means to play with
a puzzle or work with a math problem, you're

00:01:17.679 --> 00:01:25.049
building in perseverance, which is helping
you solve the next problem even if you don't

00:01:25.049 --> 00:01:27.130
end up solving this problem.

00:01:27.130 --> 00:01:31.139
So mathematics, I would say, helps people
flourish.

